 545:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   * @brief Initialize the multiprocessor mode according to the specified
 546:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   *        parameters in the UART_InitTypeDef and initialize the associated handle.
 547:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   * @param huart        UART handle.
 548:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   * @param Address      UART node address (4-, 6-, 7- or 8-bit long).
 549:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   * @param WakeUpMethod Specifies the UART wakeup method.
 550:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   *        This parameter can be one of the following values:
 551:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   *          @arg @ref UART_WAKEUPMETHOD_IDLELINE WakeUp by an idle line detection
 552:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   *          @arg @ref UART_WAKEUPMETHOD_ADDRESSMARK WakeUp by an address mark
 553:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   * @note  If the user resorts to idle line detection wake up, the Address parameter
 554:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   *        is useless and ignored by the initialization function.
 555:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   * @note  If the user resorts to address mark wake up, the address length detection
 556:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   *        is configured by default to 4 bits only. For the UART to be able to
 557:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   *        manage 6-, 7- or 8-bit long addresses detection, the API
 558:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   *        HAL_MultiProcessorEx_AddressLength_Set() must be called after
 559:Drivers/STM32WBxx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32wbxx_hal_uart.c ****   *        HAL_MultiProcessor_Init().
